    "open_questions": [
      "Which kits he played on each record: the Songsterr track names (Camco, Tama Imperialstar, Superstar, Granstar II, Artstar II, Gretsch USA Custom on Sad but True) are the transcribers' labels, not sourced; Wikipedia gives only the current Starclassic.",
      "Read the Polar Music Prize interview and the 2008 Rhythm interview directly; both are quoted here through Blabbermouth.",
      "His influences in his own words beyond Paice, Rudd, Watts and Bonham: Phil Taylor (Motörhead) is credited by Modern Drummer's obituary of Taylor, not by Ulrich.",
      "Whether Blackened's bridge, at two thirds of the tempo, is played as a metric modulation (the new beat the old dotted quarter) or simply counted slower: no source says.",
      "When he dropped the ride for the China: Wikipedia states it of his kit without a date, and Seek & Destroy's tab writes a ride in the pre-chorus."
    ]
  },
