    "roles": ["band_member", "composer", "producer"],
    "summary": "Metallica's drummer and, with James Hetfield, its writer, from his advert in The Recycler in 1981. A tennis player's son from Copenhagen who saw Deep Purple at nine, he arranged the drums round the riff: the kick doubling Hetfield's right hand, open hats washing in eighths, a rimshot backbeat, a crash on every accent. On the first four records the skank beat at full speed and two bass drums, the machine gun of One, Blackened's 7/4; from the Black Album, by his own choice, fewer notes: Enter Sandman's toms and Sad but True's weight. 'I've never been very interested in ability.'"
  },
